    "type": "question",
    "label": "6",
    "prompt": "Solve the following. $$\\frac5{x-2}-\\frac3{x+2}=\\frac{8x}{x^2-4}.$$",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$x=\\frac83$",
      "worked": "The original denominators require $x\\ne-2,2$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{5(x+2)-3(x-2)}{(x-2)(x+2)}&=\\frac{8x}{(x-2)(x+2)}\\\\5(x+2)-3(x-2)&=8x\\\\2x+16&=8x\\\\16&=6x\\\\x&=\\frac83\\end{align*}$$\n\nThis value is permitted.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
